  "worked_solution": "The formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence (in function notation) is\n\n$$\nf(n)=f(1)+(n-1)d.\n$$\n\nWe are given the first term $f(1)=-2.$ Also, the common difference of the sequence can be found as\n\n$$\nd=3-(-2)=5.\n$$\n\nSo, we substitute into the formula and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(n) & =f(1)+(n-1)d \\\\  & =-2+(n-1)(5) \\\\  & =-2+5n-5 \\\\  & =5n-7\\end{aligned}\n$$",
